## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses your ability to architect a scalable, cross-region analytics platform that enforces strict tenant isolation, data governance, and cost discipline while maintaining near real-time processing capabilities.

## Key Concepts

- Multi-region active-active design and disaster recovery strategy
- Per-tenant data isolation using storage prefixes and role-based access control
- Ingestion via Event Hubs; processing with Databricks and Delta Lake
- Data governance with Purview; encryption with customer-managed keys
- Cost optimization through auto-scaling and resource tagging

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example Spark job configuration for per-tenant partitioning
spark.conf.set("spark.sql.shuffle.partitions", "200");
spark.conf.set("spark.databricks.delta.optimizeWrite.enabled", "true");

// Read tenant-specific data
df = spark.read.format("delta")
  .load(f"abfss://tenant-{tenant_id}@storage.dfs.core.windows.net/")
  .filter(col("tenant_id") == tenant_id);

// Write with tenant partitioning
df.write.partitionBy("tenant_id")
  .format("delta")
  .mode("append")
  .save(f"abfss://processed@storage.dfs.core.windows.net/analytics");
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical Azure data pipeline design with beginner-friendly constraints, testing real-world implementation of data isolation, infrastructure as code, and CI/CD practices.

## Key Concepts

- Event Hubs for scalable event ingestion
- Per-tenant data isolation through Azure SQL schemas
- PII filtering and transformation with Azure Functions
- Infrastructure as Code using Bicep
- Continuous integration/deployment with GitHub Actions
- Cross-region disaster recovery via SQL Geo-Replication and RA-GRS
- Cost optimization: autoscaling, partition configuration, retention policies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation of routing logic for per-tenant data
function routeEvent(event){
  const tenantId = event.tenantId;
  // Filter PII and route to appropriate schema
  const filteredEvent = removePII(event);
  await writeToSQL(`tenant_${tenantId}`, filteredEvent);
}
```
